MLOps 2025: The Most Common Vector Databases You Actually  Need to Know

RAG, semantic search, embeddings, GenAI pipelines — everything runs on vector databases now.
But with so many options, which ones are really used in the industry?

Here’s the definitive list (2025 edition) 👇

---

## 🔥 Top Vector Databases Used in MLOps

### 🟩 1. Milvus (Apache 2.0)

The undisputed leader.
Built for billions of embeddings, ANN search, GPU acceleration & K8s-first deployments.

### 🟦 2. Pinecone (SaaS)

Zero infra. Zero ops.
If you just want vector search *that works*, Pinecone is the go-to.

### 🟪 3. Qdrant (Apache 2.0)

Blazing fast + powerful filtering.
Perfect for real-time RAG pipelines.

### 🟨 4. Weaviate (Apache 2.0 core)

Hybrid search → BM25 + vectors.
Highly developer friendly with amazing modules.

### 🟧 5. ChromaDB (Apache 2.0, fully open-source)

Simple. Local. Lightweight.
Most popular for LLM prototyping & quick RAG setups.

### 🟥 6. FAISS (MIT)

Not a database, but the fastest vector indexing library ever built.
Perfect for custom/offline workflows.

### 🟫 7. Redis Vector (RSAL)

Sub-millisecond retrieval.
Great for real-time inference, ranking & recommender systems.

### 🔵 8. OpenSearch Vector (Apache 2.0)

Enterprise hybrid search.
Great fit for AWS-heavy environments.

### ⚫ 9. Elasticsearch (AGPLv3 added in 2024)

Still widely used for hybrid search, but AGPL can be restrictive.
Used mainly in teams already on ELK.

---

# 🧠 When to Use What? (Super Simple Guide)

* Production RAG @ scale: Milvus / Qdrant / Pinecone
* AWS-native: OpenSearch
* Prototyping: ChromaDB
* Hybrid keyword + vector: Weaviate / OpenSearch
* Real-time apps:Redis Vector
* Custom indexing: FAISS

---

# 🔥 Final Thought

You don’t need to learn every vector DB.
Just master 2–3 based on your stack and you’re MLOps-ready for 2025
